  "_why": {
    "all takes": "s9711, regenerated from the roots re-locked to their own palette (roots_palette.py); the s9701/s9702 takes were animated from roots locked to the muddy shipped palette, so their colours did not match the idle",
    "ko (all)": "the take's last cel (CMU frame 170) smears or ghosts too often (s9701: about half the diagonals; the bruiser's south-west stood back up); frames 142 and 170 are both the body lying flat, so cel 6 holds cel 5 on every diagonal",
    "thug/jog/east": "s9901 drew the club as a detached grey squiggle in cels 0-1, which the island clean would drop; s9902 keeps it in hand in every cel"
  }
